STEP 7 — Create Docker network

Check:

docker network ls

Look for:

microservices-net

If it doesn't exist:

docker network create microservices-net

Verify:

docker network inspect microservices-net
STEP 8 — Understand the original problem

Initially Catalog had:

postgres://microapp:microapp123@127.0.0.1:5432/catalog_db

Inventory had:

postgres://microapp:microapp123@127.0.0.1:5432/inventory_db

This caused:

ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:5432

Why?

Inside Docker:

catalog container
       │
       └── 127.0.0.1
              ↓
       catalog container

It does not mean:

EC2 host

So we added:

--add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway

and changed the database host to:

host.docker.internal
STEP 9 — Verify Catalog configuration

Check source:

grep -n -E "DATABASE|DB_|postgres|5432|process.env" \
services/catalog-service/main.go

We found:

getenv("CATALOG_DB_DSN", "postgres://microapp:microapp123@127.0.0.1:5432/catalog_db?sslmode=disable")

Therefore the environment variable is:

CATALOG_DB_DSN
STEP 10 — Start Catalog

First remove an old failed container if it exists:

docker rm -f catalog-service 2>/dev/null

Start it:

docker run -d \
  --name catalog-service \
  --network microservices-net \
  --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway \
  -e CATALOG_DB_DSN="postgres://microapp:microapp123@host.docker.internal:5432/catalog_db?sslmode=disable" \
  -p 8082:8082 \
  devops-shack/catalog-service:1.0
STEP 11 — Verify Catalog

Check:

docker ps

You want:

catalog-service    Up

Check logs:

docker logs catalog-service

You should not see:

127.0.0.1:5432
connection refused

Check environment:

docker inspect catalog-service \
  --format '{{json .Config.Env}}'

You should see:

CATALOG_DB_DSN=postgres://microapp:microapp123@host.docker.internal:5432/catalog_db...
STEP 12 — Verify Inventory configuration

This was important because we initially used the wrong variable.

Run:

grep -n -E "DATABASE|DB_|postgres|5432|process.env" \
services/inventory-service/src/index.js

We found:

connectionString: process.env.INVENTORY_DB_URL ||
"postgres://microapp:microapp123@127.0.0.1:5432/inventory_db"

Therefore the correct variable is:

INVENTORY_DB_URL

Not:

INVENTORY_DB_DSN
STEP 13 — Start Inventory

Remove old container:

docker rm -f inventory-service 2>/dev/null

Run:

docker run -d \
  --name inventory-service \
  --network microservices-net \
  --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway \
  -e INVENTORY_DB_URL="postgres://microapp:microapp123@host.docker.internal:5432/inventory_db" \
  -p 8083:8083 \
  devops-shack/inventory-service:1.0
STEP 14 — Verify Inventory
docker ps

