STEP 22 — Start Frontend

First find the frontend image:

docker images

Check its Dockerfile/config to determine the port:

find . -iname "Dockerfile" -o -iname "docker-compose.yml" -o -iname "compose.yaml"

Then start it according to its actual port.

For example, if frontend listens on port 3000:

docker run -d \
  --name frontend \
  --network microservices-net \
  -p 3000:3000 \
  <frontend-image>:<tag>

If it uses nginx on port 80:

docker run -d \
  --name frontend \
  --network microservices-net \
  -p 80:80 \
  <frontend-image>:<tag>

Don't assume 3000 or 80 until we check your frontend.

